From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: incari-client <335801235+incari-client@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:10:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] services: The browser build never calls Mojang's services

Minecraft builds an online discovery service, which starts fetching
from Mojang (and retrying) the moment it's made. Where the platform
has Mojang's services off, it gets the offline one instead.

Signed-off-by: incari-client <335801235+incari-client@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/client/Minecraft.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/client/Minecraft.java
index 7117115086828a8964bdac09d8327aaf5a80f051..22cd86951c3fd35a2461577ae0ea9b0295d4b920 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/client/Minecraft.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/client/Minecraft.java
@@ -409,3 +409,5 @@
         this.offlineDeveloperMode = gameConfig.game.offlineDeveloperMode;
-        MinecraftServicesDiscoveryService discoveryService = MinecraftServicesDiscoveryService.create(this.proxy, !this.offlineDeveloperMode);
+        // Incari start: the browser build never calls Mojang's services
+        MinecraftServicesDiscoveryService discoveryService = incari.client.platform.OnlineServices.discovery(this.proxy, !this.offlineDeveloperMode);
+        // Incari end
         this.services = Services.create(discoveryService, this.gameDirectory);
